      "updated_at": null,
      "summary": "Kubernetes admission turns broad API permission into an object-level policy decision. The durable design starts with built-in controls and in-process validation, then treats webhooks as control-plane dependencies.",
      "why_it_matters": "RBAC can authorize a workload creation request without deciding whether the submitted workload meets the cluster's security contract.",
      "action": "Map the admission policies protecting each cluster, prefer built-in or in-process controls where they fit, and test webhook latency, failure policy, exclusions, and recovery before enforcing broadly.",
